{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type CustomSQLiteSerializer<TOutput, TSQLite> = Partial<{ [Key in keyof TOutput]: (value: TOutput[Key]) => Key extends keyof TSQLite ? TSQLite[Key] : never }>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/powersync-db-collection/src/definitions.ts#L56","children":[{"type":"text","value":"definitions.ts:56"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A mapping type for custom serialization of object properties to SQLite-compatible values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This type allows you to override, for keys in the input object ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput"},{"type":"text","value":"), a function that transforms\nthe value to the corresponding SQLite type ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSQLite"},{"type":"text","value":"). Keys not specified will use the default SQLite serialization."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"generics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generics"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput"},{"type":"text","value":": The input object type, representing the row data to be serialized."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSQLite"},{"type":"text","value":": The target SQLite-compatible type for each property, typically inferred from the table schema."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this type to define a map of serialization functions for specific keys when you need custom handling\n(e.g., converting complex objects, formatting dates, or handling enums)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const serializer: CustomSQLiteSerializer<MyRowType, MySQLiteType> = {\n  createdAt: (date) => date.toISOString(),\n  status: (status) => status ? 1 : 0,\n  meta: (meta) => JSON.stringify(meta),\n};","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each key maps to a function that receives the value and returns the SQLite-compatible value."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Used by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serializeForSQLite"},{"type":"text","value":" to override default serialization for specific columns."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toutput","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TOutput"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tsqlite","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSQLite"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSQLite"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"generics","text":"Generics","level":2},{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"toutput","text":"TOutput","level":3},{"id":"tsqlite","text":"TSQLite","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype CustomSQLiteSerializer<TOutput, TSQLite> = Partial<{ [Key in keyof TOutput]: (value: TOutput[Key]) => Key extends keyof TSQLite ? TSQLite[Key] : never }>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [definitions.ts:56](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/powersync-db-collection/src/definitions.ts#L56)\n\nA mapping type for custom serialization of object properties to SQLite-compatible values.\n\nThis type allows you to override, for keys in the input object (`TOutput`), a function that transforms\nthe value to the corresponding SQLite type (`TSQLite`). Keys not specified will use the default SQLite serialization.\n\n## Generics\n- `TOutput`: The input object type, representing the row data to be serialized.\n- `TSQLite`: The target SQLite-compatible type for each property, typically inferred from the table schema.\n\n## Usage\nUse this type to define a map of serialization functions for specific keys when you need custom handling\n(e.g., converting complex objects, formatting dates, or handling enums).\n\nExample:\n```ts\nconst serializer: CustomSQLiteSerializer<MyRowType, MySQLiteType> = {\n  createdAt: (date) => date.toISOString(),\n  status: (status) => status ? 1 : 0,\n  meta: (meta) => JSON.stringify(meta),\n};\n```\n\n## Behavior\n- Each key maps to a function that receives the value and returns the SQLite-compatible value.\n- Used by `serializeForSQLite` to override default serialization for specific columns.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TOutput\n\n`TOutput` *extends* `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n### TSQLite\n\n`TSQLite` *extends* `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: CustomSQLiteSerializer\ntitle: CustomSQLiteSerializer\n---\n\n```ts\ntype CustomSQLiteSerializer<TOutput, TSQLite> = Partial<{ [Key in keyof TOutput]: (value: TOutput[Key]) => Key extends keyof TSQLite ? TSQLite[Key] : never }>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [definitions.ts:56](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/powersync-db-collection/src/definitions.ts#L56)\n\nA mapping type for custom serialization of object properties to SQLite-compatible values.\n\nThis type allows you to override, for keys in the input object (`TOutput`), a function that transforms\nthe value to the corresponding SQLite type (`TSQLite`). Keys not specified will use the default SQLite serialization.\n\n## Generics\n- `TOutput`: The input object type, representing the row data to be serialized.\n- `TSQLite`: The target SQLite-compatible type for each property, typically inferred from the table schema.\n\n## Usage\nUse this type to define a map of serialization functions for specific keys when you need custom handling\n(e.g., converting complex objects, formatting dates, or handling enums).\n\nExample:\n```ts\nconst serializer: CustomSQLiteSerializer<MyRowType, MySQLiteType> = {\n  createdAt: (date) => date.toISOString(),\n  status: (status) => status ? 1 : 0,\n  meta: (meta) => JSON.stringify(meta),\n};\n```\n\n## Behavior\n- Each key maps to a function that receives the value and returns the SQLite-compatible value.\n- Used by `serializeForSQLite` to override default serialization for specific columns.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TOutput\n\n`TOutput` *extends* `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n### TSQLite\n\n`TSQLite` *extends* `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n"}
